{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And bless himself in his heart.</b> He accepts the oath with his mouth yet blesses himself in his heart in order to annul it." "<b>To the end that the watered be swept away with the thirsty.</b> And the reason he accepts the oath with his mouth is so that he may add his own soul — watered and sated in all its desires — to the congregation of El the thirsty, separated from physical desires, in order to rejoice with them in their blessings."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:30.315185574Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}